# LANChat peers allowed to use this discovery server.
#
# One peer ID per line. Each user prints theirs with:
#
#   lanchat identity show
#
# A peer ID is 32 characters (a-z and 2-7) derived from the user's identity
# key; it changes only if the user resets their identity. Everything after
# '#' is a comment and blank lines are ignored.
#
# The server re-reads this file within a few seconds of a change. Removing a
# line revokes access: the peer is refused on its next refresh and is no
# longer shown to others. Deleting the whole file refuses everyone.
#
# Examples (remove the leading '#' and use real IDs):
#
# abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz234567   # alice - laptop
# 234567abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz   # bob - workstation
